# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md; pypinyin.md
# shows how this ledger applies them. Current support is Python 2.7 and
# Python >=3.4,<4 (README.rst:15; setup.py:75,90-105). CHANGELOG.rst:413-414
# drops the guarantee for 2.6/3.3 despite the broader installer bound. CPython,
# PyPy and explicitly supported IronPython are admitted (CHANGELOG.rst:542;
# compat.py:12-17). Python 2 branches remain in scope; their builtin callees
# use Python 3 counterparts (unicode -> str, str -> bytes). The .pyi stubs next to the
# modules give the parameter types (B2, B4).
# Converters: public DefaultConverter bodies also run on the package-created
# _v2UConverter, _neutralToneWith5Converter and _toneSandhiConverter subclasses
# that inherit them. B1 admits these receivers even where the package does not
# call an inherited body. Client-created combined mixin classes remain opaque.

